  "prefLabel": "Occ 102.01 American Occupational Therapy Association (AOTA)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Occ 102.01 “American Occupational Therapy Association (AOTA)” means the entity recognized as the national professional organization of occupational therapists, occupational therapy assistants, and students enrolled in occupational therapy education programs, or its successor.\n\nSource. #8572, eff 1-26-05; ss by #13081, eff 7-31-20 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Occ 100); ss by #14366, eff 9-9-25",
